--- NOTES ---
This is the minimal fix (Approach A). It adds empty stub struct definitions in the
#else branch of AesWorldProfilingTrace.h so that TUniquePtr<FAesTracePayloadScope>
has a complete type to delete in all build configurations.

Files changed:
  1. Source/AesWorldProfiling/Public/AesWorldProfilingTrace.h  (+5 lines)
  2. Source/AesWorldProfiling/Private/AesWorldProfilingTrace.cpp  (+1 line)

The fix preserves the existing architecture -- AesLodSystem continues to depend on
AesWorldProfiling, and the PayloadTraceScope member remains in the request classes.
In non-debug builds, the TUniquePtr will simply hold a pointer to an empty struct
(which will always be nullptr since creation is guarded by #if WITH_EARTH_DEBUGGER).
